Northbridge High — Packet Tracer (fictional school LAN)
Not the Ballymoney rack. Real 108S is unmanaged / one flat LAN.

---
What it is in real words
A small school network: IT office, teachers, students on separate VLANs so kids cannot reach the IT server. One router does the routing between VLANs (router-on-a-stick). DHCP hands out addresses. An ACL is a firewall rule on the student side.

---
Kit in the sim
R1 = 2911 router (the "core" / default gateway)
SW-ACCESS = 2960 switch (classroom/office access switch)
IT-PC, Staff-PC, Student-PC
SRV1 = school file/AD stand-in, same VLAN as IT
Did not build 40 suite PCs — one student PC stands in for the suite

---
Cables
Straight-through copper
IT-PC -> Fa0/1
Staff-PC -> Fa0/2
Student-PC -> Fa0/3
SRV1 -> Fa0/4
R1 Gi0/0 -> SW Gi0/1 (this one is the trunk)
PCs/server went green first. R1 stayed red until no shutdown on Gi0/0.

---
Switch (access + trunk)
VLAN 10 IT
VLAN 20 STAFF
VLAN 30 STUDENTS
Access port = one VLAN only (like a wall socket in one department)
Trunk = one cable carrying many VLANs (switch to router), 802.1Q tags
Fa0/1 and Fa0/4 = VLAN 10
Fa0/2 = VLAN 20
Fa0/3 = VLAN 30
Gi0/1 = trunk

---
Router-on-a-stick
One physical port, subinterfaces:
Gi0/0.10 = 192.168.10.1  VLAN 10
Gi0/0.20 = 192.168.20.1  VLAN 20
Gi0/0.30 = 192.168.30.1  VLAN 30
.1 = default gateway for that VLAN
DHCP pools IT / STAFF / STUDENTS, exclude .1
PCs set to DHCP

---
Addresses we actually saw
SRV1 started 0.0.0.0 (no lease) — ipconfig on a server is ipconfig not "ip config"
Then DHCP: SRV1 = 192.168.10.3  gw 192.168.10.1
Students = 192.168.30.x
Staff = 192.168.20.x
IT = 192.168.10.x

---
ACL (access control list = packet filter / basic firewall)
On Gi0/0.30 in (traffic from students hitting the router)
deny 192.168.30.0/24 -> 192.168.10.0/24
permit anything else
Staff on .20 not in that ACL so they can still reach IT

Tests
Student ping 192.168.30.1 = OK
Student ping 192.168.10.1 = destination host unreachable (blocked)
Student ping 192.168.10.3 SRV1 = blocked
Staff ping 192.168.20.1 = OK
Staff ping 192.168.10.1 = OK
Staff ping 192.168.10.3 = OK (first ping sometimes times out = ARP)
IT to SRV1 = same VLAN, does not use that ACL

